// AUTO-GENERATED by the DS audit inventory sweep (2026-08-25). Do not hand-edit.
// Source: peanut-ui feat/design-system @ 843df91b — swept at 7ae13804 by 10 parallel finders,
// one per DS category, then a mechanical re-count of every row (the adversarial pass).
// Refreshed to 843df91b (the phase-2 styling cleanup, 16 commits, 236 product files) by a delta
// pass: one probe per row over the 7ae13804 corpus and the 843df91b corpus, with the difference
// added to the swept number. A delta is method-independent, so it carries a row forward without
// having to re-derive that row's original bespoke grep. 93 rows moved; the rest are unchanged.
// 165 rows carry a prose or glob key ("inline recipe: text-sm + font-bold", "--color-avatar-*")
// that no single probe reproduces — those numbers still date from 7ae13804.
// Not re-inventoried: PageStack (64), Section (23), ListGroup (9), TitleBlock (1) and
// ActiveCardGate (3) are new primitives from this base and have no row yet.
// Replaces the 2026-06-26 giga-sweep. That method is recoverable from mono commit f9346907,
// file inbox/ds-consolidation-audit/README.md (the folder itself was deleted 2026-08-06).
// Method: usages = call sites over src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}, minus /dev routes, __tests__ and
// *.test.* — the live-product lens the 2026-06 pass used. A component row counts JSX call sites
// with the ERE `<Name([^A-Za-z]|$)`. The `|$` is load-bearing: Prettier writes multi-line
// `<Name\n  prop=…`, and the 2026-06 sweep missed that form and called three live components dead.
// A token or CSS-class row counts word-bounded occurrences of its key. Every number here was
// machine-measured from the row's own grep and re-measured a second time at assembly, so no count
// is hand-typed.
// LAYER_STATS.distinct keeps its 2026-06 meaning — distinct implementations in the wild, not row
// counts: tokens = keys declared in the globals.css @theme block, styles = distinct inline
// typographic recipes, every other layer = its inventory rows. `target` is a design goal, not a
// measurement, so it is carried over unchanged.

